        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carlos Santana, O.C. Smith, Marker Starling\n- Organizations: Santana\n- Products: Inner Secrets, Stormy, For Once In My Life, I'm Willing\n- Concepts: rock and Latin American music fusion\n\nFacts:\n- Carlos Santana was born on July 20, 1947.\n- Carlos Santana is a Mexican and American musician.\n- Carlos Santana first became famous in the late 1960s and early 1970s with his band Santana.\n- Santana pioneered a fusion of rock and Latin American music.\n- O.C. Smith covered the song \"Stormy\" in 1968 on his Columbia album \"For Once In My Life.\"\n- Inner Secrets is the ninth studio album by Santana.\n- Santana covered the song \"Stormy\" in 1978 on the album \"Inner Secrets.\"\n- Marker Starling covered the song \"Stormy\" on the 2016 album \"I'm Willing.\"",
